2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240009Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240165Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240393Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240606Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240677Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240842Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4240944Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4241059Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4241345Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4241511Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4241595Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4241815Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4241959Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4242068Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4242348Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4242625Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4243157Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4243579Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4243661Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4243998Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4244415Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4244640Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4245040Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4245361Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4245430Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4245583Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4245675Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4247312Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4248377Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4248549Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4248931Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4311640Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4312185Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4312748Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4313300Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4313666Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4313750Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4313944Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4314061Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4314854Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4315714Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4316311Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4316983Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:50.4317152Z 
